      "sample_index": 1,
      "text": "To find the area of the square, we need to determine the length of one of its sides. We are given two expressions for the length of the edge of the square: \\(4x - 15\\) meters and \\(20 - 3x\\) meters. Since both expressions represent the same length, we can set them equal to each other and solve for \\(x\\).\n\n\\[\n4x - 15 = 20 - 3x\n\\]\n\nFirst, we add \\(3x\\) to both sides of the equation to combine the \\(x\\) terms on one side:\n\n\\[\n4x + 3x - 15 = 20\n\\]\n\nThis simplifies to:\n\n\\[\n7x - 15 = 20\n\\]\n\nNext, we add 15 to both sides to isolate the term with \\(x\\):\n\n\\[\n7x = 35\n\\]\n\nNow, we divide both sides by 7 to solve for \\(x\\):\n\n\\[\nx = 5\n\\]\n\nWith \\(x = 5\\), we can substitute this value back into one of the expressions for the edge length to find the length of the side of the square. We can use either \\(4x - 15\\) or \\(20 - 3x\\). Let's use \\(4x - 15\\):\n\n\\[\n4(5) - 15 = 20 - 15 = 5\n\\]\n\nSo, the length of the side of the square is 5 meters. The area \\(A\\) of a square is given by the square of the length of one of its sides:\n\n\\[\nA = 5^2 = 25\n\\]\n\nTherefore, the area of the square is \\(\\boxed{25}\\) square meters.",
