      "sample_index": 6,
      "text": "To find the area of the square, we first need to determine the length of one of its sides. According to the problem, the length of one side of the square can be expressed in two different ways: \\(4x - 15\\) meters or \\(20 - 3x\\) meters. Since both expressions represent the same side length, we can set them equal to each other and solve for \\(x\\):\n\n\\[\n4x - 15 = 20 - 3x\n\\]\n\nNext, we solve this equation step by step. First, we add \\(3x\\) to both sides to combine the \\(x\\) terms on one side:\n\n\\[\n4x + 3x - 15 = 20\n\\]\n\nThis simplifies to:\n\n\\[\n7x - 15 = 20\n\\]\n\nThen, we add 15 to both sides to isolate the term with \\(x\\):\n\n\\[\n7x = 35\n\\]\n\nFinally, we divide both sides by 7 to solve for \\(x\\):\n\n\\[\nx = 5\n\\]\n\nNow that we have the value of \\(x\\), we can substitute it back into one of the expressions for the side length to find the actual length of the side. We use the expression \\(4x - 15\\):\n\n\\[\n4(5) - 15 = 20 - 15 = 5\n\\]\n\nSo, the length of one side of the square is 5 meters. The area of a square is given by the square of the length of its side. Therefore, the area \\(A\\) is:\n\n\\[\nA = 5^2 = 25\n\\]\n\nThus, the area of the square is \\(\\boxed{25}\\) square meters.",
