    "text": "To find the area of the square, we first need to determine the length of one of its sides. According to the problem, the length of an edge of the square can be expressed in two different ways: \\(4x - 15\\) meters or \\(20 - 3x\\) meters. Since both expressions represent the same length, we can set them equal to each other and solve for \\(x\\):\n\n\\[\n4x - 15 = 20 - 3x\n\\]\n\nTo isolate \\(x\\), we first add \\(3x\\) to both sides of the equation:\n\n\\[\n4x + 3x - 15 = 20\n\\]\n\nThis simplifies to:\n\n\\[\n7x - 15 = 20\n\\]\n\nNext, we add 15 to both sides to further isolate the term with \\(x\\):\n\n\\[\n7x = 35\n\\]\n\nNow, we divide both sides by 7 to solve for \\(x\\):\n\n\\[\nx = 5\n\\]\n\nWith \\(x = 5\\), we can substitute this value back into either expression for the side length of the square to find the actual length of the side. We use the expression \\(4x - 15\\):\n\n\\[\n4(5) - 15 = 20 - 15 = 5\n\\]\n\nSo, the length of one side of the square is 5 meters. The area \\(A\\) of a square is given by the square of the length of its side:\n\n\\[\nA = 5^2 = 25\n\\]\n\nTherefore, the area of the square is \\(\\boxed{25}\\) square meters.",
